<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thrace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thrace is a historical region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, bounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a>, and now divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. It was home to the Thracian peoples and the Odrysian kingdom before becoming a Roman province in 46 CE. Its position on the approaches to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> made it a battleground for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thrace.jpg" alt="Thrace" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Factuarius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thrace_region.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
